# BuildKit prefers `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` over a root `.dockerignore`.
#
# The Dockerfile copies the WHOLE repo, because `bun.lock` describes every workspace member and a
# partial copy makes `--frozen-lockfile` refuse. This file keeps that cheap — but it may only
# exclude things that are NOT workspace members. Excluding `examples/*/apps` removed those
# members' `package.json` files, which is the same refusal by another route: bun resolves the
# workspace from the manifests on disk, so a missing manifest is a lockfile that "changed".
#
# The rule: ignore artifacts and secrets, never a manifest.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Artifacts. `.x/` holds the embedded Postgres data directory — hundreds of files, none of them
# meaningful in a container that talks to a real server.
**/.x
**/dist
**/build
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/coverage

.git
.github

# Never bake an environment into an image: one artifact deploys everywhere and the values arrive
# from the platform.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Same shape, different file, and the one this list was missing: an `.npmrc` carries a registry auth
# token, so any that exists here is somebody's local credential. This Dockerfile is `COPY . .` over
# the WHOLE repo and `.github/workflows/deploy-social-demo.yml` builds it with
# `cache-to: type=gha,mode=max` — an untracked `.npmrc` on a contributor's box would land in a layer
# and be pushed to a cache the whole repository can read. The other three ignore files beside this
# one have carried the line since 2026-08-19.
**/.npmrc
